# Ink deploy canary. Claude rewrites this file after a substantial change; InkWatch (scripts\ink-watch.ps1)
# notices the new modification time and runs scripts\ink-push.ps1: commit + push, Firestore rules, Worker.
# subject: becomes the commit subject; everything after body: becomes the commit body.
last_tick: 2026-09-22T00:00:00Z
subject: Sales landing pages: marketing home + author page builder
body:
- New signed-out marketing page at ink.jacobsiler.com: hero, feature grid, plan comparison (early access = free), then sign-in -- replaces the bare login box.
- New "Pages" section in the app: authors build sign-up pages (opt-in form, adds readers to the list) or sales pages (headline + one off-site CTA button), using the same formatting toolbar as letters.
- shared/render.js gains renderLandingPage() -- reuses the same markdown parser as emails (so the same **bold**/*italic*/etc. all work) but wraps it in a webpage shell instead of an email shell.
- Worker: GET/POST /p/:slug serves the published page and captures sign-ups; POST /pages/:id/publish|unpublish claims/releases the public slug (a new pageSlugs collection, same pattern as the existing join-page slugs). Page docs themselves are read/written directly from the app like campaigns -- firestore.rules' existing authors/{uid}/{collection} wildcard already covers them; only pageSlugs needed a new rule.
- Support address ink@jacobsiler.com wired into the marketing footer and the delete-list dialog (forwards to Jacob via Cloudflare Email Routing).
- Verified: renderLandingPage() output (signup + buy kinds, markdown formatting) with direct Node tests; full JS syntax check on index.html and worker/src/index.js.
